 },
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "BeatStep User's Manual v1.0.1 (Arturia)",
   "url": "https://downloads.arturia.com/products/beatstep/manual/BeatStep_Manual_1_0_1_EN.pdf",
   "note": "ch. 8 default settings (CNTRL presets): encoders 1–16 CC 7 74 71 76 77 93 73 75 114 18 19 16 17 91 79 72, Absolute, Global channel; pads 1–8 notes 44–51, pads 9–16 notes 36–43, Gate; STOP / PLAY send MMC Stop (01) / Play (02) to device 127. §3.1: Global MIDI channel defaults to 1. §2.2: 16 endless encoders + the Level/Rate encoder (master level in CNTRL mode), 16 velocity- and pressure-sensitive pads; pads numbered 1–8 on the top row, 9–16 below (front-panel diagram)"
  },
  {
   "title": "Ableton Live 12 MIDI Remote Script BeatStep (decompiled; non-official)",
   "url": "https://github.com/gluon/AbletonLive12_MIDIRemoteScripts/blob/main/BeatStep/BeatStep.py",
   "note": "same encoder CCs except encoder 1 (it re-programs the unit by SysEx and puts encoder 1 on CC 10); pad rows 44–51 (top) and 36–43 (bottom)"
  },
  {
   "title": "DrivenByMoss BeatstepControllerDefinition.java (Bitwig; non-official)",
   "url": "https://github.com/git-moss/DrivenByMoss/blob/master/src/main/java/de/mossgrabers/controller/arturia/beatstep/BeatstepControllerDefinition.java",
   "note": "port name \"Arturia BeatStep\""
  }
 ],
 "notes": "CNTRL mode (red pads) with the factory preset, Global channel 1. The big Level/Rate encoder is not modelled: the manual's default table does not list it (it \"controls the master level by default\"); if it also sends CC 7 it will move encoder 1 on screen. STOP / PLAY send MMC SysEx and are not modelled (SysEx stays off). SEQ mode plays the step sequencer on the sequencer channel instead — not modelled. The encoders are endless but send absolute values in the default preset. Pad pressure: poly aftertouch is followed automatically if the unit sends it. The original BeatStep only — the BeatStep Pro is a different device and is not matched.",
